  message: "Satisfied. Merged as PR #1858 (dev 258809980b; two commits: the fix, and a CI follow-up). Option (a), keeping the claim: the runtime loader _load_st_model_offline_first is cache-only (a miss raises EmbeddingsUnavailable naming install-embeddings), _ensure_hf_offline_for_cached_models forces HF_HUB_OFFLINE on every runtime load, and sketch_embeddings.fetch_embedding_models is the one place a model is fetched, run by install-embeddings (also when the library is already installed) and add-extras in a fresh interpreter; install-embeddings --check now fails when the weights are missing. runtime-cli-no-network, the spec, both READMEs and SECURITY.md updated; the I/O allowlist finding is gone. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE on merged dev, the premise check's own repro re-run: stub sentence_transformers (logs each construction, raises OSError), empty HF_HOME, HF_HUB_OFFLINE unset, proxy 127.0.0.1:9, `hypergumbo sketch` on the same 2-file fixture -> exit 0, 5 constructions, EVERY one {local_files_only: true, HF_HUB_OFFLINE: \"1\"} (before: 10, each cache-only attempt followed by a {local_files_only: false, HF_HUB_OFFLINE: null} download-allowed retry); stderr carries the degradation warning naming 'hypergumbo install-embeddings ... downloads the model weights into $HF_HOME'. check-self-claims: 18 unchanged. BEHAVIOUR CHANGE, stated: `pip install 'hypergumbo[embeddings]'` without install-embeddings now sketches without embeddings and says to run it. NOT checked: a real download through install-embeddings (no network used). PROCESS NOTE: the first CI run failed two install tests that passed locally only because this machine's HF cache holds both models; tests now pin the cache state, and the fix was verified with HF_HOME pointed at an empty directory."  # 74b7
